  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Step One: Generate Your Data with AI\r\n\r\n### Do This:\r\n\r\n1. The squishy card example from the last level is uploaded in this activity.\r\n\r\n\r\n2. Ask AI to generate arrays for your data.\r\n   * You should have one array for each part of your UI.\r\n   * Each array should have at least 3 items.\r\n   \r\n\r\n3. Check your arrays:\r\n   * Do all arrays have the same number of items?\r\n   * Does each index represent one complete item?\r\n\r\n### Reminder:\r\n- Each array stores one type of information\r\n- The same index across arrays should match\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Step Two: Display One Card\r\n###Do This: \r\n1. Create variables that store the values at index 0 from each array.\r\n\r\n2. Use those variables to call `createCard()`.\r\n\r\n3. Run your code and check:\r\n   * Does one card display correctly?\r\n   * Do all parts of the card match?\r\n\r\n### Reminder:\r\n- Index 0 represents one complete card\r\n- All values at the same index should match\r\n",
    "submittable": "false",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "false",
    "disable_edit_run_for_submission": "false",
